    {
      "id": "gloss_b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -156.0,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 392,
      "height": 250.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 471619988,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1470197912,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "RoPE  —  rotary position embedding: spins\nQ & K by an angle set by position, so the\nmodel feels token order without a separate\nposition table.\n\nRMSNorm  —  rescales each vector to unit\nsize (cheaper than LayerNorm, no mean\nsubtraction) to keep training stable.\n\nSwiGLU  —  gated feed-forward: SiLU(gate)\n× up. The gate lets the layer choose what\ninformation passes through.\n\nWeight-tying  —  the embedding matrix and\nthe output head share ONE matrix, saving\n~8M params and improving quality.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RoPE  —  rotary position embedding: spins\nQ & K by an angle set by position, so the\nmodel feels token order without a separate\nposition table.\n\nRMSNorm  —  rescales each vector to unit\nsize (cheaper than LayerNorm, no mean\nsubtraction) to keep training stable.\n\nSwiGLU  —  gated feed-forward: SiLU(gate)\n× up. The gate lets the layer choose what\ninformation passes through.\n\nWeight-tying  —  the embedding matrix and\nthe output head share ONE matrix, saving\n~8M params and improving quality.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cap",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -170.0,
      "y": 1092,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 168,
      "angle": 0,
